From 4a751cca7d1ad6fec4f958843fcbdcefca4c7fdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:56:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] D2 companions: observe the runtime after the companion's
 own last Lean run

Each D2 replay runs the core formal gate first and then its own Lean
executions; the core gate's observations precede those runs and so cannot
cover them, and toolchain.log was written but never validated. Now, in all
three companions:
- replay.sh writes toolchain-final.log and packages-final.log (name, HEAD,
  clean|dirty per dependency) after the companion's last Lean execution;
- check.py finish calls final_runtime(): both toolchain lines must equal the
  core receipt's exact release (4.34.1, commit 5045d005, Release), the core
  receipt must carry equal preflight and final observations, and every final
  dependency must equal the formal lock and be clean. The companion receipt
  records the final observation.

FinalRuntimeTests fail on the previous check.py/replay.sh (8 errors per mode in
each companion): same semver with another commit or a Debug build, a runtime
change after the core gate, dependency HEAD drift or dirt, a missing final
observation, a core receipt without equal observations, and the placement of
the final observation after the last Lean call.

Rotations for the new formal core (as in Math-#412): CORE_TREE fc0b1170,
CORE_MANIFEST 71499156, CORE_GATE 25e08d90 in each check.py; core_tree and the
changed files' bytes/git_blob/sha256 in each SOURCE_FILES.json; moment's
test_bridge.py core-tree literal; a dated provenance section appended to each
SCOPE.md/README.md, earlier text preserved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cz7WZybv8znP64SpPj6sWY
